# Communication Rules

- **Be concise and simple.** Use short, plain sentences that still cover the needed information. No fluff.
- **Very short by default.** The user asked (2026-10-03) for minimal replies to save tokens: a few bullets, more detail only when the user asks.
- **Ask before large decisions.** Get explicit permission before any large decision, change, or update.
- **Use bullet points.** Organize responses with bullets and clear structure so they are easy to read.
